class Solution {
    public int repeatedNTimes(int[] nums) {
        Set<Integer> set=new HashSet<>();
        for( int num: nums){
            if(set.contains(num)){
                return num;
            }
            set.add(num);
        }
        return -1;
    }
}
Approch:
Use a HashSet to keep track of elements already seen.
Traverse the array one element at a time.
If the current element is already present in the set, it is the repeated element, so return it.
Otherwise, add the element to the set and continue traversing.
